      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Finalize customer scripts, education materials, and escalation rules.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M18",
            "speaker_id": 65624,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've completed a first draft of the customer sales and advisory script, which you can find in A2. This is for task T2. I'd appreciate feedback from 24897 and 556038 on technical accuracy, and from 89356 on compliance, especially regarding promises of returns.",
            "mentions": [
              24897,
              556038,
              89356
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 24897,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "Thanks 65624, this is a great start. The flow is logical and customer-friendly. On page 3, for the 'Balanced Growth Portfolio', let's rephrase 'aims to deliver' to 'is designed with the objective of'. It's a subtle but important compliance distinction to manage expectations. Otherwise, technically accurate.",
            "mentions": [
              65624
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 17558,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "This script is very helpful. It covers the most common questions. What should we do if a customer asks for a product that isn't in our catalogue?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 65624,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Good question. We should probably capture that as a lead or feedback, but not try to sell it. That brings up the topic of escalation rules for complex questions, which is task T11.",
            "mentions": [
              17558
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 89356,
            "reply_to": "M18",
            "text": "The script says we need to give customers a leaflet. Is that a legal requirement?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 556038,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "It's not strictly a legal requirement for all products, but it's best practice and our internal policy to provide a Key Information Document. That's what T3 is about - creating those simplified info sheets. The script A2 is fine as is, it correctly references providing materials.",
            "mentions": [
              89356
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3",
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 24897,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Let's define the escalation rules now. I propose we create A7 with the following criteria: \n1. Any question about personal tax implications -> Escalate. \n2. Any request for a customized portfolio -> Escalate. \n3. Any technical questions about market mechanics not covered in the T3 sheets -> Escalate. \nEscalations go to the on-call trader via a dedicated chat channel, with a 2-hour response SLA during store hours.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7",
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 65624,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "That's perfect. Clear, simple, and actionable for the store staff. I'll update A2 with the wording change suggested by 24897. If everyone is happy with that and the escalation rules, we can get these signed off.",
            "mentions": [
              24897
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 17558,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "The rules in A7 make sense to me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 556038,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "The escalation criteria are robust. I approve.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
